    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">1</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Schema Warm-Up</h2>
                <p>Use the table explorer, schema view, and ERD before writing queries.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.1.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Primary keys</span>
                </div>
                <p>Name the three tables and identify the primary key in each one.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.2.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Schema levels</span>
                </div>
                <p>State which schema level would show: the entities and their relationships, the data types and keys, and the indexing or storage choices.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.1.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Relationships</span>
                </div>
                <p>Describe the relationship between <code>STUDENT</code> and <code>LOAN</code>, and between <code>BOOK</code> and <code>LOAN</code>. Include cardinality and the role of referential integrity.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.1.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Evaluation</span>
                </div>
                <p>Give one benefit and one limitation of storing this data in a relational database rather than in separate spreadsheets.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">2</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Retrieve and Filter</h2>
                <p>Build confidence with <code>SELECT</code>, <code>FROM</code>, and <code>WHERE</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">SELECT *</span>
                </div>
                <p>Display every row and column from <code>STUDENT</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Specific columns</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show only <code>FirstName</code>, <code>LastName</code>, and <code>TutorGroup</code> for students in tutor group <code>12B</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">AND / OR</span>
                </div>
                <p>List the titles and genres of books where the genre is <code>Science</code> or <code>Technology</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">WHERE</span>
                </div>
                <p>Find every loan record where <code>ReturnStatus</code> is <code>Overdue</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">BETWEEN</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show books published between <code>2020</code> and <code>2024</code> inclusive.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">LIKE</span>
                </div>
                <p>Return the titles and authors of books whose title contains the word <code>Code</code>.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">3</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Sort the Result Set</h2>
                <p>Control how the rows are presented after filtering.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">DISTINCT</span>
                </div>
                <p>List every distinct value that appears in <code>ReturnStatus</code>, sorted alphabetically.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">ORDER BY DESC</span>
                </div>
                <p>Display book title, author, and published year, sorted newest to oldest. If two books share a year, sort those alphabetically by title.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">ORDER BY ASC</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show student names grouped by tutor group, then by last name.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">4</span>
            <div>
                <h2>First Joins</h2>
                <p>Use foreign keys to combine tables into one result set.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 2 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>Join <code>LOAN</code> to <code>STUDENT</code> and show which students currently have a book <code>On Loan</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 2 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>Join <code>LOAN</code> to <code>BOOK</code> to list the titles, authors, and due dates for every overdue loan.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 3 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show each current loan with student full name, book title, author, and due date. Sort by due date first.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.1.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Integrity</span>
                </div>
                <p>Explain why a loan row with <code>StudentID = 9999</code> should be rejected in a relational database with referential integrity turned on.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">5</span>
            <div>
                <h2>DDL and DML</h2>
                <p>Complete these last. They change the live workspace.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">DDL</span>
                </div>
                <p>Create a new table called <code>REVIEW</code> with columns <code>ReviewID</code>, <code>BookID</code>, <code>Rating</code>, and <code>Comment</code>. Make <code>ReviewID</code> the primary key and link <code>BookID</code> back to <code>BOOK</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.3</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">INSERT</span>
                </div>
                <p>Insert one review for <code>BookID 2002</code> with a rating and a short comment.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.3</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">UPDATE</span>
                </div>
                <p>Update loan <code>3006</code> so that its <code>ReturnStatus</code> becomes <code>Returned</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.3</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">DELETE</span>
                </div>
                <p>Delete the review row you added, then check that the table is empty again.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="sql-sheet-note">Reset the dataset afterwards by reopening the worksheet launch link or selecting <code>School Library</code> again in the playground.</p>
    </section>

